      "narrative": "The tavern's copper lamps sway gently as you approach the woman in the charcoal coat. She had been nursing a small cup of something dark, her gaze fixed on the shuttered window. When your boots scrape the floorboards, she turns \u2014 and there's a flicker of recognition, as if she was already expecting you.\n\nShe sets her cup down. \"The Ash Gate, is it? Everyone's asking, these days.\"\n\nYou lean in, ready to catch every detail. But the words tangle somewhere between her telling and your hearing. She speaks of the lock mechanism \u2014 something about a *triple-tumbler sequence* and the *Kestrel Guild's seal* \u2014 and your mind snags on a memory of a different gate, somewhere in the northern woods, and suddenly you've lost the thread. You catch yourself nodding along, but the specifics have slipped through your fingers like smoke.\n\nMara pauses, studies your face, and her eyes narrow just a fraction.\n\n\"You're not taking this in, are you?\"\n\n<ref_entity>..."
