      "narrative": "Mara Venn leans back, her sharp eyes still fixed on you with that same narrowed suspicion. She's quiet for a moment, then lets out a short breath \u2014 not quite a sigh, more a dismissal.\n\n\"The lockwright,\" she says flatly. \"That's who maintained it. Name doesn't matter.\"\n\nBut it does matter. You know it matters. You *just* discussed this with someone \u2014 the lockwright who kept the Ash Gate's mechanism running for years, sworn to the Kestrel Guild. The name sits at the edge of your mind, a shape you can almost touch.\n\nAnd then your own tongue betrays you.\n\n\"Tor\u2014\" you start, and Mara's eyebrow lifts. You stop. You can't pull the full name. It's *right there* \u2014 Toran something. Toran Vex. The nervous clerk with the ink-stained cuffs, sitting not ten feet from you at the bar.\n\nBut when you open your mouth again, all that comes out is: \"The lockwright. Right.\"\n\nMara's expression goes cold. She doesn't believe you forgot. She thinks you're *playing* at something.\n\n\"Look,\" she says, her voice dropping, \"if you're going to fish for information you already have, we're done here.\" She reaches for her cup, deliberately turning her shoulder toward you.\n\n<ref_entity entity_id=\"mara-venn\" dialogue_indices=\"[1,2,3]\" dialogue_emotions=\"[\"suspicious\", \"flat\", \"cold\"]\"></ref_entity>\n<ref_entity entity_id=\"toran-vex\" alias_used=\"Toran Vex\"></ref_entity>..."
