      "narrative": "The question hangs between you. Mara's fingers tighten on her cup, and for a moment you think she'll shut you down entirely. But something in your persistence \u2014 or maybe just the directness of the ask \u2014 makes her pause.\n\nShe sets the cup down. Her jaw works once.\n\n\"Old Bram,\" she says. \"The ferryman. He ran the passage. Had the key, took the payments, worked the boat.\"\n\nShe says it like the name should mean something to you. Old Bram. The ferryman who carried people through the Ash Gate \u2014 until he didn't.\n\n\"He's dead now, in case you hadn't heard.\" Her voice turns brittle. \"Found facedown at the landing three weeks ago. Boat still rots there.\"\n\nShe watches you, waiting to see if this lands or if you'll ask for a name you already have.\n\n<ref_entity entity_id=\"mara-venn\" dialogue_indices=\"[1,2]\" dialogue_emotions=\"[\"flat\", \"brittle\"]\"></ref_entity>..."
