      "narrative": "The door of the Copper Finch swings shut behind you, cutting off the low murmur of the tavern. The morning air carries the smell of wet stone and woodsmoke \u2014 the rain has stopped, but the cobbles still glisten.\n\nA short lane leads east, past shuttered houses and a single guttering streetlamp, and then the buildings fall away. The ground opens into a flat stretch of mud and gravel, and there \u2014 standing alone against a pale grey sky \u2014 is the Ash Gate.\n\nIt's a cracked black arch, maybe fifteen feet high, set into nothing. No wall flanks it. No road leads through it, just the trampled mud of a crossing that's seen little use. On the other side of the arch, the world looks the same \u2014 grey sky, damp ground \u2014 but something about the angle of the light feels *wrong*, like the air beyond the arch breathes at a different pace.\n\nThe Grey Hind, Old Bram's ferry boat, sits beached twenty feet from the water's edge. A narrow river \u2014 dark, slow-moving \u2014 curves past the gate's base, and a simple wooden dock juts out into it, half-rotted.\n\nA figure stands near the boat. Travel-stained cloak, hood down, studying the hull with the patient attention of someone waiting.\n\n<ref_entity entity_id=\"ash-gate\" alias_used=\"Ash Gate\"></ref_entity>\n<ref_entity entity_id=\"old-bram\" alias_used=\"Old Bram\"></ref_entity>\n\n<spawn_object object_id=\"grey-hind\" name=\"Grey Hind\" description=\"Old Bram's ferry boat, beached and rotting at the landing\"></spawn_object>\n<spawn_object object_id=\"ash-gate-mechanism\" name=\"Ash Gate mechanism\" description=\"The gate's lock and mechanism, visible on the inner face of the arch\"></spawn_object>\n\n<change_location location_name=\"Ash Gate\" description=\"A cracked black arch standing alone against grey sky, a rotting ferry boat beached nearby\"></change_location>..."
