      "narrative": "Your voice carries across the flat ground \u2014 \"Old Bram!\" \u2014 and hangs in the damp air for a long moment.\n\nNothing answers.\n\nThe river laps against the rotting dock. A bird calls somewhere distant, thin and unanswered. The figure near the boat turns at the sound of your voice, curious but not alarmed.\n\nThere is no reply because Old Bram is dead. Has been for three weeks. The ferryman isn't coming to this call or any other.\n\nThe silence stretches, and the Ash Gate stands black against the grey sky, indifferent.\n\nThe courier by the boat \u2014 a woman in a travel-stained cloak \u2014 watches you with an unreadable expression. She's young, maybe late twenties, with a sharp face and dark hair pulled back. A leather satchel is slung across her chest, worn at the edges.\n\n\"Won't get an answer,\" she says, not unkindly. \"He's been dead since before I got here.\"\n\n<ref_entity entity_id=\"sable-quill\" dialogue_indices=\"[1]\" dialogue_emotions=\"[\"flat\"]\"></ref_entity>..."
