      "narrative": "You drop to a crouch beneath the cracked arch, your fingers brushing the damp stone. The ground here is churned \u2014 mud displaced in uneven ridges, as if something \u2014 or someone \u2014 moved through recently and in a hurry. The pattern isn't random. It's deliberate movement, fast and purposeful, the kind of track a person leaves when they're running or dragging weight.\n\nAnd there, on the stone beneath the arch itself: faint scratches. Long, parallel gouges in the black rock, too regular to be natural. Something heavy was dragged through here. Recently. The scratches catch the grey light at an angle, fresh enough that the edges haven't softened.\n\nYou look closer at the gate's mechanism \u2014 the lock visible on the inner face of the arch. Beside the keyhole, you spot a small indentation. Not a second keyhole. Something else. A recess, smooth-edged, the size of your thumbnail. No standard key would fit it.\n\nThe courier Sable Quill has moved a few steps closer, watching you work. She doesn't speak, but her attention is sharp.\n\n<ref_entity entity_id=\"ash-gate-mechanism\"></ref_entity>\n<ref_entity entity_id=\"sable-quill\"></ref_entity>..."
